NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000328 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000329 "=head1 NAME"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000330 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000331 "Data::Clean - Clean data structure"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000332 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000333 "=head1 VERSION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000334 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000335 "This document describes version 0.508 of Data::Clean (from Perl distribution Data-Clean), released on 2022-08-28."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000336 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000337 "=head1 SYNOPSIS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000338 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000339 " use Data::Clean;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000340 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000341 " my $cleanser = Data::Clean->new("
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000342 "     # specify how to deal with specific classes"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000343 "     'DateTime'     => [call_method => 'epoch'], # replace object with its epoch"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000344 "     'Time::Moment' => [call_method => 'epoch'], # replace object with its epoch"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000345 "     'Regexp'       => ['stringify'], # replace $obj with \"$obj\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000346 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000347 "     # specify how to deal with all scalar refs"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000348 "     SCALAR         => ['deref_scalar'], # replace \\1 with 1"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000349 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000350 "     # specify how to deal with circular reference"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000351 "     -circular      => ['clone'],"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000352 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000353 "     # specify how to deal with all other kinds of objects"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000354 "     -obj           => ['unbless'],"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000355 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000356 "     # recurse into object"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000357 "     #'!recurse_obj'=> 1,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000358 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000359 "     # generate cleaner with debugging messages"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000360 "     #'!debug'      => 1,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000361 " );"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000362 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000363 " # to get cleansed data"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000364 " my $cleansed_data = $cleanser->clone_and_clean($data);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000365 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000366 " # to replace original data with cleansed one"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000367 " $cleanser->clean_in_place($data);"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000368 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000369 "=head1 DESCRIPTION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000370 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000371 "This class can be used to process a data structure by replacing some forms of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000372 "data items with other forms. One of the main uses is to clean \"unsafe\" data,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000373 "e.g. clean a data structure so it can be encoded to JSON (see"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000374 "L<Data::Clean::ForJSON>, which is a thin wrapper over this class)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000375 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000376 "As can be seen from the example, you specify a list of transformations to be"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000377 "done, and then this class will generate an appropriate Perl code to do the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000378 "cleansing. This class is faster than the other ways of processing, e.g."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000379 "L<Data::Rmap> (see L<Bencher::Scenarios::DataCleansing> for some benchmarks)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000380 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000381 "=for Pod::Coverage ^(command_.+)$"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000382 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000383 "=head1 METHODS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000384 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000385 "=head2 new(%opts) => $obj"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000386 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000387 "Create a new instance."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000388 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000389 "Options specify what to do with certain category of data. Option keys are either"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000390 "reference types (like C<HASH>, C<ARRAY>, C<SCALAR>) or class names (like"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000391 "C<Foo::Bar>), or C<-obj> (to match all kinds of objects, a.k.a. blessed"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000392 "references), C<-circular> (to match circular references), C<-ref> (to refer to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000393 "any kind of references, used to process references not handled by other"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000394 "options). Option values are arrayrefs, the first element of the array is command"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000395 "name, to specify what to do with the reference/class. The rest are command"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000396 "arguments."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000397 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000398 "Note that arrayrefs and hashrefs are always walked into, so it's not trapped by"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000399 "C<-ref>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000400 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000401 "Default for C<%opts>: C<< -ref => 'stringify' >>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000402 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000403 "Option keys that start with C<!> are special:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000404 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000405 "=over"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000406 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000407 "=item * !recurse_obj (bool)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000408 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000409 "Can be set to true to to recurse into objects if they are hash- or array-based."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000410 "By default objects are not recursed into. Note that if you enable this option,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000411 "object options (like C<Foo::Bar> or C<-obj>) won't work for hash- and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000412 "array-based objects because they will be recursed instead."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000413 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000414 "=item * !clone_func (str)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000415 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000416 "Set fully qualified name of clone function to use. The default is to get the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000417 "value of the environment C<PERL_DATA_CLEAN_CLONE_FUNC> or use the default"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000418 "C<Clone::PP::clone>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000419 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000420 "The clone module (all but the last part of the C<!clone_func> value) will"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000421 "automatically be loaded using C<require()>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000422 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000423 "=item * !debug (bool)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000424 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000425 "If set to true, will generate code to print debugging messages. For debugging"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000426 "only."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000427 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000428 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000429 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000430 "Available commands:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000431 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000432 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000433 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000434 "=item * ['stringify']"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000435 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000436 "This will stringify a reference like C<{}> to something like C<HASH(0x135f998)>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000437 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000438 "=item * ['replace_with_ref']"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000439 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000440 "This will replace a reference like C<{}> with C<HASH>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000441 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000442 "=item * ['replace_with_str', STR]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000443 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000444 "This will replace a reference like C<{}> with I<STR>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000445 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000446 "=item * ['call_method' => STR]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000447 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000448 "This will call a method named I<STR> and use its return as the replacement. For"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000449 "example: C<< DateTime->from_epoch(epoch=>1000) >> when processed with C<<"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000450 "[call_method => 'epoch'] >> will become 1000."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000451 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000452 "=item * ['call_func', STR]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000453 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000454 "This will call a function named I<STR> with value as argument and use its return"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000455 "as the replacement."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000456 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000457 "=item * ['one_or_zero']"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000458 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000459 "This will perform C<< $val ? 1:0 >>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000460 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000461 "=item * ['deref_scalar_one_or_zero']"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000462 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000463 "This will perform C<< ${$val} ? 1:0 >>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000464 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000465 "=item * ['deref_scalar']"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000466 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000467 "This will replace a scalar reference like \\1 with 1."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000468 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000469 "=item * ['unbless']"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000470 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000471 "This will perform unblessing using L<Function::Fallback::CoreOrPP::unbless()>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000472 "Should be done only for objects (C<-obj>)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000473 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000474 "=item * ['die']"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000475 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000476 "Die. Only for testing."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000477 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000478 "=item * ['code', STR]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000479 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000480 "This will replace with I<STR> treated as Perl code."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000481 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000482 "=item * ['clone', INT]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000483 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000484 "This command is useful if you have circular references and want to expand/copy"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000485 "them. For example:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000486 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000487 " my $def_opts = { opt1 => 'default', opt2 => 0 };"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000488 " my $users    = { alice => $def_opts, bob => $def_opts, charlie => $def_opts };"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000489 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000490 "C<$users> contains three references to the same data structure. With the default"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000491 "behaviour of C<< -circular => [replace_with_str => 'CIRCULAR'] >> the cleaned"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000492 "data structure will be:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000493 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000494 " { alice   => { opt1 => 'default', opt2 => 0 },"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000495 "   bob     => 'CIRCULAR',"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000496 "   charlie => 'CIRCULAR' }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000497 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000498 "But with C<< -circular => ['clone'] >> option, the data structure will be"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000499 "cleaned to become (the C<$def_opts> is cloned):"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000500 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000501 " { alice   => { opt1 => 'default', opt2 => 0 },"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000502 "   bob     => { opt1 => 'default', opt2 => 0 },"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000503 "   charlie => { opt1 => 'default', opt2 => 0 }, }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000504 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000505 "The command argument specifies the number of references to clone as a limit (the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000506 "default is 50), since a cyclical structure can lead to infinite cloning. Above"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000507 "this limit, the circular references will be replaced with a string"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000508 "C<\"CIRCULAR\">. For example:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000509 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000510 " my $a = [1]; push @$a, $a;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000511 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000512 "With C<< -circular => ['clone', 2] >> the data will be cleaned as:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000513 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000514 " [1, [1, [1, \"CIRCULAR\"]]]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000515 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000516 "With C<< -circular => ['clone', 3] >> the data will be cleaned as:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000517 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000518 " [1, [1, [1, [1, \"CIRCULAR\"]]]]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000519 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000520 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000521 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000522 "=head2 $obj->clean_in_place($data) => $cleaned"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000523 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000524 "Clean $data. Modify data in-place."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000525 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000526 "=head2 $obj->clone_and_clean($data) => $cleaned"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000527 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000528 "Clean $data. Clone $data first."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000529 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000530 "=head1 ENVIRONMENT"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000531 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000532 "=over"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000533 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000534 "=item * PERL_DATA_CLEAN_CLONE_FUNC"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000535 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000536 "String. Set default for C<!clone_func> option."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000537 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000538 "=item * LOG_CLEANSER_CODE => BOOL (default: 0)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000539 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000540 "Can be enabled if you want to see the generated cleanser code. It is logged at"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000541 "level C<trace> using L<Log::ger>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000542 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000543 "=item * LINENUM => BOOL (default: 1)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000544 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000545 "When logging cleanser code, whether to give line numbers."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000546 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000547 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000548 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000549 "=head1 HOMEPAGE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000550 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000551 "Please visit the project's homepage at L<https://metacpan.org/release/Data-Clean>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000552 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000553 "=head1 SOURCE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000554 ""
